      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62dee7096d6050449f776f77|full_name} Having worked on JXL the past year, stumbling onto your comment just now was a nice surprise haha.\n\nUnfortunately I'd imagine plumbing new image formats into Unity would be too much of a nightmare. (Though, Udon loading does support WebP which Unity doesn't...)\n\nRunning a quick test anyway, a 4K photo goes from 9 MB PNG to 7 MB JXL in 25 ms on a single thread. So it'd definitely be fast enough, also goes down to 6 MB at 500 ms on the second fastest setting. A nice bonus is that JXL has extra channel support, so depth maps or the multi-layer camera could save to a single image while still being smaller than a normal PNG.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
